  "objective": "Give Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge the strongest honest Riemann-Roch and vanishing substrate available for the committed Picard representability route. Cluster P is the Euler-characteristic ledger, section-drop results, and uniform H1 vanishing needed downstream. AJC already has a substantial sorry-free adelic lane including RiemannRoch/Adelic/ChiLedger.lean; the sibling Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild has a broader sorry-free 17,792-line RiemannRoch development across 63 files. In particular AJCR RiemannRoch/UniformVanishing.lean proves a single-field bounded vanishing core \u2014 it does NOT by itself supply field-extension uniformity or global generation, and conflating those three is the specific error this task exists to avoid.\n\nDECIDE PROVENANCE THEOREM BY THEOREM: reuse AJC code, port an AJCR result, adapt its argument, or rederive it in the AJC abstractions. Report that provenance honestly and do not promise a mechanical port. A predecessor assessment judged that auditing AJCR for portability decides where the next two months go, more than any single proof would \u2014 so the audit IS deliverable work, not a preliminary.\n\nREAD THE CAVEAT BEFORE TRUSTING AJC RR: much of the adelic lane is conditional in the STATEMENT on the closed chi-ledger or a peel datum. Read scripts/axiom-frontier.lean sections 6b/6d before treating any of it as available. Report #print axioms for every major landed result, measured at a synthesis site rather than at the declaration \u2014 a theorem quantifying over a gate instance reports clean axioms as stated and only picks up sorryAx where the instance is synthesised.\n\nFILE SCOPE, NARROWED 2026-07-28 TO AVOID A LIVE COLLISION. You own AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/** EXCEPT RiemannRoch/WeilDivisor.lean, which belongs to the concurrently-running ajc-pic0av lane along with the AJC.rr.principal milestone (principal divisors have degree zero). DO NOT EDIT WeilDivisor.lean. If your substrate work would materially help close that leaf, post the lemma on the AJC conversation thread (I-0493) and let ajc-pic0av land it. You may read AJCR freely but must never modify it. Also off-limits: Picard/**, Jacobian.lean, AbelJacobi.lean, Cohomology/**, the root import roll-up, and blueprint files.\n\nWORKSPACE STATE YOU ARE JOINING, so you do not misdiagnose it: seven other lanes are live. The ROOT BUILD IS CURRENTLY RED on ajc-fbcs in-flight Cohomology/ edit \u2014 that is expected, it is their file, and it is not yours to fix. Build your own target (lake build AlgebraicJacobian.RiemannRoch... or the narrowest lake env lean) rather than the root, and do not report another lanes red build as your own failure. ajc-gate and ajc-truth are FINISHED, so the old instruction to notify them is void: post to the AJC thread I-0493 instead, and note that ajc-etale-pic has already landed the etale-sheafified Picard seam (Picard/PicEtSheaf.lean, sorry-free) and DELETED the false leaf hasRationalPoint_of_curve \u2014 do not build against a rational-point hypothesis.\n\nCONCURRENCY. Commit via a private index with compare-and-swap, never a bare git commit against the ledger: ajc-etale-pic hit exactly that race this morning and had to repair two commits whose diffs did not match their messages (recipe on I-0493). Verify after every commit that git status --porcelain shows no stray deletions and that your commit touched only your paths.\n\nDONE MEANS: the strongest reachable cluster-P statements are present under AJC-compatible hypotheses; focused Lean checks pass; no new anonymous or misleading sorry boundaries; axioms reported; and every remaining gap distinguishes single-field vanishing, extension-uniformity, and global generation precisely. A fresh-context ground review before any terminal done claim.",
